---
/* Privacy notice, version 1.0 (2026-11-26). DRAFT for legal review: every <mark class="legal-todo">
   is a fact only the responsible entity's legal team can supply. Written from what the site really
   does (checked 2026-11-26): no accounts, no forms of its own, no cookies, no analytics, three
   preference items in the visitor's own browser, third-party hosts GitHub (site and API) and
   Hugging Face (map explorer layers). Change this text only with a new version number and date. */
import LegalPage from '../components/layout/LegalPage.astro'

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="What personal data the MOSAIC website handles, who receives it, and how to exercise your rights."
  version="1.0"
  effective="2026-11-26"
>
  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    MOSAIC is an initiative of the CGIAR Multifunctional Landscapes Science Program. The entity
    responsible for the personal data described here is
    <mark class="legal-todo">[RESPONSIBLE ENTITY: legal name, registered address, telephone]</mark>.
  </p>
  <p>
    For any question or request about your personal data, write to
    <mark class="legal-todo">[PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL]</mark>.
    This notice covers the MOSAIC website and the MOSAIC API. Websites and data files we link to
    have their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Visiting the website</h2>
  <p>
    The website has no user accounts, no sign-in, no forms of its own, no cookies, no analytics
    and no advertising. We do not build profiles of visitors.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting.</strong> The website and the API are served by GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.,
      United States). To deliver each page, GitHub's servers receive your IP address and technical
      details of the request, under the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
      MOSAIC does not receive these logs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Map explorers.</strong> When you open a landscape's map explorer, some map layers
      are loaded from Hugging Face (Hugging Face, Inc., United States) and from the GitHub Pages
      site of the explorer's author. Those services receive your IP address, under the
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/privacy">Hugging Face privacy policy</a> and GitHub's
      statement. Nothing is loaded from them until you open a map.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Settings kept in your browser.</strong> The site remembers three choices in your
      own browser: light or dark theme and whether the map panel is folded (kept until you clear
      your browser's site data), and your last catalog search (deleted when you close the tab).
      They are not cookies, they never leave your device, and they are set only when you make the
      choice. You can delete them at any time from your browser's settings.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Contact details shown in the catalog</h2>
  <p>
    A dataset's page may show the name, organization and work email of a contact person, so that
    users can cite the data and ask for access. These details come from the person or their
    institution when the dataset was registered, or from the dataset's own documentation.
    Legal basis: <mark class="legal-todo">[LEGAL BASIS: consent of the contact person, or legitimate interest in attributing scientific data]</mark>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are named in the catalog, you can ask us at any time to correct your details, replace
    them with an institutional address, or remove them.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Writing to us or contributing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Email.</strong> When you write to MOSAIC, we use your address and message only to
      answer you and handle your request. We keep them for
      <mark class="legal-todo">[RETENTION PERIOD]</mark>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>GitHub issue forms.</strong> Registering a dataset or reporting a problem through
      GitHub creates a public issue on GitHub, visible to anyone, under GitHub's own terms and
      privacy statement. Do not include personal data you do not want published there.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Who receives personal data</h2>
  <p>
    Only the services named above: GitHub and Hugging Face as hosts, and
    <mark class="legal-todo">[EMAIL PROVIDER, e.g. Microsoft 365 for CGIAR mail]</mark> for email.
    We do not sell personal data or share it for advertising. These services are based in the
    United States. <mark class="legal-todo">[SAFEGUARDS FOR INTERNATIONAL TRANSFERS]</mark>
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to know what personal data we hold about you, to correct or update it, to have
    it deleted, to object to its use, and to withdraw any consent you gave. Write to
    <mark class="legal-todo">[PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL]</mark> with the subject
    “MOSAIC privacy request”, say who you are and what you ask for. Requests are free.
  </p>
  <p>
    We answer requests for information within 10 working days and requests to correct or delete
    within 15 working days. If we need longer, we tell you why and when you will have an answer.
    You can also complain to
    <mark class="legal-todo">[DATA PROTECTION AUTHORITY or other complaint route]</mark>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The website is meant for researchers, institutions and decision-makers. It is not directed at
    children and we do not knowingly collect their data.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    Each version of this notice has a number and a date. We publish a substantial change on this
    page before it takes effect. See also the <a href={`${base}/terms`}>Terms of use</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
